# Balance data

Spec §32.5 requires that balance values live in Godot resources, **not** in unit
scripts. The `.tres` is what the game reads.

| Resource class | Script | Instances |
|---|---|---|
| `CargoData` | `scripts/data/cargo_data.gd` | `data/cargo_data.tres` |
| `DefenderData` | `scripts/data/defender_data.gd` | `data/defenders/` ×4 |
| `EnemyData` | `scripts/data/enemy_data.gd` | `data/enemies/` ×2 |
| `SpellData` | `scripts/data/spell_data.gd` | `data/spells/` ×3 |
| `ControlProfileData` | `scripts/data/control_profile_data.gd` | `data/profiles/` ×4 |
| `TestSeedData` | `scripts/data/test_seed_data.gd` | `data/seeds/` ×3 |
| `MapRouteData` | `scripts/data/map_route_data.gd` | `data/map_route.tres` |
| `DefenderTuning` | `scripts/data/defender_tuning.gd` | `data/defender_tuning.tres` |

**Every one of these is already filled from the specification tables**, including the
resources for systems that have no behaviour yet. That is why the remaining
milestones are behaviour only — you should almost never need to create a resource,
only read one.

## Changing a number

The spec table and the `.tres` must agree. When you change one, change the other and
say which you treated as authoritative. A silent divergence between them is a bug —
there is already one open, on cargo Fast speed; see
[docs/status.md](mdc:docs/status.md).

## Two that need care

**`data/map_route.tres`** drives the entire generated map. After changing the route
shape, re-run the calculator so the length and turn demand you quote are the ones
Godot actually bakes:

```sh
python3 tools/road_calc.py --target 9000 --wavelength 2800
```

Route length is asserted at 9000 px by the smoke test. A round zone offset can also
break convex decomposition — see [engine traps](mdc:.cursor/rules/020-godot-traps.mdc).

**`data/profiles/*.tres`** carries `ControlProfileData.implemented`, which is what
greys out P2–P4 on the selection screen instead of silently running P1. Flip a flag
only when that profile genuinely works end to end.
